  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-[[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-4-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-6-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenoxy)oxane-3,4,5-triol, is shown to interact with the CD70 antigen through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of three different compounds: Scalarolide, Xestamine E, and Jbir-34, all of which are themselves targets of the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. This suggests that the compound may exert its biological effect through the activation or modulation of this subunit, which in turn influences the CD70 antigen. The evidence is consistent across three distinct targets, indicating a potential mechanism involving the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 as a mediator. The final scores from the three paths are similar, suggesting a strong and reliable relationship between the compound and the CD70 antigen, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
